        {
          "type": "kotak",
          "title": "About punctuality",
          "items": [
            "In Georgia, nine o'clock for official business — offices, doctors, classes — really means nine o'clock.",
            "Nine o'clock for social plans — dinner, meeting friends — usually means somewhere between nine and half past, and nobody will see it as a problem.",
            "If you're late, one sentence is enough: **ბოდიში, დავაგვიანე.** No long explanation needed.",
            "⚠️ A dinner invitation at a Georgian home almost never has an end time. Don't make other plans afterward."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "One word worth noting now, even though it'll only be useful later: **დრო** (dro) means \"time\". *დრო გაქვს?* (do you have time?) is the most common way to invite someone, and unit 15 builds a whole conversation on it."
        }
      ]
    }
